        "id": 1966126
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-07T22:00:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hello.\nhttps://www.arib.or.jp/english/html/overview/doc/STD-T63v9_10/5_Appendix/Rel5/33/33203-5c0.pdf states 3gpp should pad the key with zeroes at the end.\n\ntrailing zeroes apparently do not impact computation at all, so it really just is a way to work around the limitation and they\u0027ve standardized something less secure than it should be.. But it\u0027s not like we can do anything about that!\n\nAnyway, it works for me™ so I think we can abandon this patch. Thank you both!",
      "parentUuid": "700215c5_aae20a56",
